LOCATIONS={
'san-francisco':('San Francisco','From a commercial lease to an ownership disagreement, a San Francisco business may need advice that connects its day-to-day operations with a longer-term legal objective. Our published office is at 28 Geary St, Suite 650.','For a local business inquiry, identify the contracting entities and whether the issue concerns an agreement, an existing dispute, a tax notice, or an investigation. That helps us route the matter before requesting records.'),
'san-francisco-county':('San Francisco County','Owners and professionals in San Francisco County can face connected company and individual legal questions. We assess who needs representation and whether separate interests must be considered.','Tell us whether the inquiry is for the company, an owner, or both. For tax matters, identify the taxpayer and the agency; for disputes, identify the parties and any pending case.'),
'san-jose':('San Jose','A San Jose business entering a new commercial relationship or addressing a contract breakdown needs a strategy that reflects the documents and the operating goal. We help connect contract work with dispute planning.','If the matter involves a business agreement, describe whether it is unsigned, in operation, or already disputed. For an employer inquiry, make clear that you are contacting us on behalf of the business.'),
'santa-clara':('Santa Clara','Ownership arrangements and commercial relationships can change as a Santa Clara company develops. We review agreements and disputes with attention to how responsibilities and decisions are documented.','For an ownership matter, identify the entity, the owners involved, and whether the aim is to update an agreement, resolve a disagreement, or negotiate an exit.'),
'santa-clara-county':('Santa Clara County','Businesses across Santa Clara County may need coordinated advice when a departure, disputed contract, or ownership decision affects several parts of the company. We consider those connections when defining the engagement.','Let us know whether related proceedings or adviser relationships already exist. With authorization, we can coordinate legal work with accounting advisers or existing counsel within an agreed scope.'),
'palo-alto':('Palo Alto','A business owner in Palo Alto may be reviewing a significant agreement, documenting ownership, or evaluating a commercial dispute. We focus on clear terms and a practical plan for the decisions ahead.','Before a consultation about a proposed transaction, note the signing target, the parties, and the terms that remain unresolved. Do not send confidential deal documents through the website form.'),
'sunnyvale':('Sunnyvale','For a Sunnyvale business, a dispute over performance or confidential information can affect ongoing operations. We evaluate the record and the available options alongside the company’s practical needs.','Describe the business relationship and whether a demand, termination notice, or lawsuit has been received. Identify urgent dates without including sensitive company information in the form.'),
'fremont':('Fremont','Commercial contracts, supplier relationships, and ownership decisions can create legal needs for Fremont businesses. We help evaluate terms before a commitment and address disputes when expectations diverge.','For a contract inquiry, identify whether the concern is payment, delivery, performance, or termination. A short timeline and the desired business outcome help frame the initial review.'),
'oakland':('Oakland','Oakland businesses and owners can turn to the firm for commercial disputes, agreements, tax matters, and white-collar defense. We assess the particular issue rather than assuming that every business concern calls for litigation.','If you received a tax notice or investigation request, identify the agency and the response date. If you are responding to a business claim, note whether a case has already been filed.'),
'alameda-county':('Alameda County','For clients in Alameda County, an issue may cross city boundaries or involve several business entities. We clarify the parties and their roles before developing the scope of representation.','Include the company’s name, the other parties, and the location of any pending proceeding in an initial inquiry. Our only published office is in San Francisco; meetings are arranged with the firm.'),
'redwood-city':('Redwood City','Redwood City owners may need counsel for business agreements, a planned purchase or sale, or a dispute that could disrupt operations. We help identify unresolved obligations and the practical objective.','For a purchase or sale inquiry, state whether you are the buyer or seller and how far negotiations have progressed. We can discuss coordination with other advisers after reviewing the fit.'),
'san-mateo-county':('San Mateo County','We serve San Mateo County businesses and individuals in matters within our business, tax, and defense practices. Some engagements involve both a company’s position and an owner’s separate concerns.','Clarify who is seeking representation and whether the matter involves a business tax issue, an individual tax issue, or both. The identity of the taxpayer and the agency helps define the legal work.'),
'morgan-hill':('Morgan Hill','Owners in Morgan Hill may seek advice on commercial leases, operating agreements, or the terms of a business relationship. We review those documents in the context of the company’s goals and risks.','For a commercial property inquiry, describe the business use and the agreement involved. This practice does not market residential or neighborhood property disputes.'),
'gilroy':('Gilroy','Gilroy businesses facing a disputed payment, ownership change, or tax notice need clarity about the next step. We help assess the issue and whether it calls for transaction work, negotiation, or a contested proceeding.','Provide a short summary and any deadline. When the amount or procedure points toward small claims, we can discuss the separate scope of advice and appeal representation available through that practice.'),
'monterey-county':('Monterey County','We serve Monterey County clients in accepted business, tax, and defense matters from our San Francisco office. Representation and meeting arrangements are discussed during intake.','If the issue involves an investigation or court matter, include the agency or court and the next date. Do not assume an inquiry confirms an appearance or that the firm can meet an immediate deadline.')}
